295
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:47,819
C'mon...

296
00:22:47,940 --> 00:22:48,660
nice and easy.

297
00:22:49,700 --> 00:22:50,039
Slowly now,

298
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:50,880
take it easy.

299
00:23:09,559 --> 00:23:10,819
What's going on with her?

300
00:23:11,380 --> 00:23:12,119
Master,

301
00:23:13,380 --> 00:23:14,599
the smoke she inhaled

302
00:23:14,599 --> 00:23:15,740
caused massive oxygen loss

303
00:23:16,099 --> 00:23:17,420
to her brain.

304
00:23:17,900 --> 00:23:19,900
A deep clot formed,

305
00:23:20,940 --> 00:23:22,200
causing amnesia.

306
00:23:30,779 --> 00:23:32,119
When will she get her memory back?

307
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:35,480
Surgery is out of the question.

308
00:23:36,079 --> 00:23:36,579
All we can do

309
00:23:36,579 --> 00:23:38,319
is let the clot dissolve.

310
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:40,059
It might take

311
00:23:40,059 --> 00:23:41,400
a few months,

312
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:42,960
or...

313
00:23:45,259 --> 00:23:46,740
she might never remember.

314
00:23:56,519 --> 00:23:57,960
Ma'am, you're up!

315
00:24:01,559 --> 00:24:02,460
Easy does it...

316
00:24:11,279 --> 00:24:12,240
Are you

317
00:24:12,779 --> 00:24:14,259
feeling any better?

318
00:24:32,440 --> 00:24:34,299
Master had these flowers put here.

319
00:24:34,599 --> 00:24:36,500
Fresh ones brought in

320
00:24:36,619 --> 00:24:37,880
every morning!

321
00:24:41,039 --> 00:24:42,559
Who was

322
00:24:44,160 --> 00:24:45,500
that man earlier?

323
00:24:45,700 --> 00:24:47,400
That's Master Yu,

324
00:24:47,559 --> 00:24:48,599
your husband!

325
00:24:48,859 --> 00:24:50,220
Second-in-command

326
00:24:50,220 --> 00:24:51,579
of the entire Nanhuai army!

327
00:24:53,059 --> 00:24:54,039
Husband?

328
00:25:08,559 --> 00:25:09,940
Then why can't I

329
00:25:11,400 --> 00:25:13,660
recall anything?

330
00:25:16,099 --> 00:25:17,259
He brought you home

331
00:25:17,259 --> 00:25:18,420
after the fire.

332
00:25:18,859 --> 00:25:20,759
Told us you inhaled too much smoke.

333
00:25:21,940 --> 00:25:23,579
You've been out cold for two years.

334
00:25:27,240 --> 00:25:28,660
Two years...

335
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:31,920
The doctors said

336
00:25:31,920 --> 00:25:33,359
you'd never wake up,

337
00:25:33,839 --> 00:25:35,539
yet he insisted on marrying you.

338
00:25:35,799 --> 00:25:37,140
He told his father

339
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:38,759
he'd spend his life taking care of you

340
00:25:38,839 --> 00:25:40,500
no matter what!

341
00:25:42,259 --> 00:25:43,339
You have no idea

342
00:25:43,339 --> 00:25:44,539
how much he loves you!

343
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:45,940
He never

344
00:25:45,940 --> 00:25:47,900
left your side for two years.

345
00:25:48,240 --> 00:25:50,900
Rubbing your limbs, bathing you...

346
00:25:51,480 --> 00:25:52,019
He wouldn't

347
00:25:52,019 --> 00:25:53,660
trust the staff with herbs.

348
00:25:53,900 --> 00:25:57,599
He brewed every dose himself!

349
00:26:02,579 --> 00:26:03,140
See that cot?

350
00:26:03,440 --> 00:26:05,299
He slept here just to

351
00:26:05,440 --> 00:26:06,740
be by your side.

352
00:26:18,779 --> 00:26:19,460
[Master,]

353
00:26:20,779 --> 00:26:22,180
[the smoke she inhaled]

354
00:26:22,180 --> 00:26:23,220
[caused massive oxygen loss]

355
00:26:23,599 --> 00:26:24,940
[to her brain.]

356
00:26:25,299 --> 00:26:27,339
[A deep clot formed,]

357
00:26:27,940 --> 00:26:29,279
[causing amnesia.]

358
00:26:34,779 --> 00:26:35,579
Master!

359
00:26:36,599 --> 00:26:37,400
Master!

360
00:26:38,059 --> 00:26:39,420
She's asking for you!

361
00:27:05,759 --> 00:27:07,000
Are you really my husband?

362
00:27:10,559 --> 00:27:11,259
I am.

363
00:27:14,880 --> 00:27:16,519
Tang told me everything.

364
00:27:17,359 --> 00:27:18,559
You've been

365
00:27:18,680 --> 00:27:20,519
taking care of me...

366
00:27:26,859 --> 00:27:28,680
I can't remember any of it.

367
00:27:29,359 --> 00:27:30,680
I've got no way

368
00:27:31,579 --> 00:27:32,140
to repay

369
00:27:32,140 --> 00:27:33,680
such devotion.

370
00:27:46,019 --> 00:27:47,359
You're my wife.

371
00:27:48,359 --> 00:27:49,500
You don't owe me a thing.

372
00:27:51,579 --> 00:27:52,779
Having you back

373
00:27:53,660 --> 00:27:54,640
is the greatest blessing

374
00:27:54,640 --> 00:27:55,720
in the world.

375
00:27:58,799 --> 00:27:59,660
So...

376
00:28:00,200 --> 00:28:01,220
how did we

377
00:28:01,220 --> 00:28:02,519
meet?

378
00:28:04,519 --> 00:28:06,579
[It's a miracle she woke up at all.]

379
00:28:06,900 --> 00:28:08,799
[Any shock could]

380
00:28:08,799 --> 00:28:11,359
[prove fatal.]

381
00:28:13,279 --> 00:28:15,019
After you graduated,

382
00:28:16,299 --> 00:28:17,299
you took a job

383
00:28:17,700 --> 00:28:19,759
copying scripts at the Grand Vernal.

384
00:28:21,359 --> 00:28:22,960
We kinda rubbed each other

385
00:28:23,440 --> 00:28:24,940
the wrong way at first.

386
00:28:25,980 --> 00:28:27,480
Then fate stepped in.

387
00:28:28,740 --> 00:28:29,500
We weathered

388
00:28:29,500 --> 00:28:30,500
storms together...

389
00:28:33,859 --> 00:28:34,920
and eventually...

390
00:28:36,519 --> 00:28:37,779
we fell in love.

391
00:28:45,299 --> 00:28:47,539
What about my family?

392
00:28:51,680 --> 00:28:52,960
Your father

393
00:28:54,440 --> 00:28:55,559
remarried long ago.

394
00:28:57,079 --> 00:28:58,539
He wasn't around when you grew up.

395
00:28:59,279 --> 00:29:00,680
He runs finance

396
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:03,039
out in Southeast Asia,

397
00:29:03,359 --> 00:29:04,740
though I've sent word

398
00:29:05,599 --> 00:29:06,500
letting him know

399
00:29:06,500 --> 00:29:07,180
you're alright.

400
00:29:09,099 --> 00:29:10,359
About your mother...

401
00:29:18,240 --> 00:29:19,279
What about

402
00:29:21,259 --> 00:29:22,160
her?

403
00:29:27,359 --> 00:29:29,259
She suffered from a lung disease.

404
00:29:30,240 --> 00:29:31,680
The surgery couldn't

405
00:29:32,619 --> 00:29:34,299
save her.

406
00:29:36,559 --> 00:29:37,819
She passed away long ago.

407
00:29:50,039 --> 00:29:50,980
You've still got me.

408
00:29:52,440 --> 00:29:53,839
I will never leave you.

409
00:30:13,500 --> 00:30:14,480
It's fine if nothing

410
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:15,680
comes back yet.

411
00:30:17,059 --> 00:30:17,859
It's OK.

412
00:30:19,299 --> 00:30:20,599
We've got the rest of our lives.

413
00:30:32,500 --> 00:30:33,500
It's cooled off.

414
00:30:34,099 --> 00:30:34,900
Here, take it.

415
00:31:17,299 --> 00:31:18,980
Yes! Yes!

416
00:31:19,359 --> 00:31:20,480
You gotta be kidding me?!

417
00:31:20,700 --> 00:31:28,759
C'mon, roll high!

418
00:31:36,420 --> 00:31:37,480
[Are you really my husband?]

419
00:31:38,359 --> 00:31:38,859
[I am.]

420
00:31:40,259 --> 00:31:42,460
[What about my family?]

421
00:31:46,859 --> 00:31:49,960
[Your father remarried long ago.]

422
00:31:51,579 --> 00:31:52,900
[About your mother...]

423
00:31:55,119 --> 00:31:56,140
[She passed away long ago.]

424
00:32:29,660 --> 00:32:31,059
Drowning your sorrows solves nothing.

425
00:32:32,359 --> 00:32:36,240
Reality waits when you sober up.

426
00:32:40,339 --> 00:32:41,140
Zhongfang,

427
00:32:45,460 --> 00:32:47,119
did I cause all this?

428
00:32:49,500 --> 00:32:50,480
If I hadn't stopped her

429
00:32:50,480 --> 00:32:51,640
at the port,

430
00:32:54,640 --> 00:32:56,440
would she still be whole?

431
00:32:58,900 --> 00:33:00,059
That wasn't your fault.

432
00:33:02,259 --> 00:33:03,440
Still,

433
00:33:05,160 --> 00:33:06,700
keeping the truth from her...

434
00:33:08,700 --> 00:33:09,539
have you thought this through?

435
00:33:14,660 --> 00:33:15,720
I know what I'm doing.

436
00:33:17,759 --> 00:33:19,160
Call me selfish.

437
00:33:22,859 --> 00:33:25,000
I know lying to her is wrong,

438
00:33:26,859 --> 00:33:28,559
but I'll be damned

439
00:33:32,920 --> 00:33:34,880
if I lose her.

440
00:33:36,779 --> 00:33:37,859
Where do you go

441
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:40,720
from here?

442
00:33:47,900 --> 00:33:48,779
I see this as

443
00:33:48,779 --> 00:33:50,119
God's mercy.

444
00:33:53,839 --> 00:33:55,480
A clean slate for us

445
00:33:58,900 --> 00:34:00,099
to start over.

446
00:34:09,139 --> 00:34:10,639
Look at the men at those tables.

447
00:34:12,940 --> 00:34:14,739
Risking everything on a

448
00:34:14,940 --> 00:34:16,079
single throw.

449
00:34:17,099 --> 00:34:18,219
Life is

450
00:34:18,860 --> 00:34:19,840
far heavier

451
00:34:19,840 --> 00:34:20,940
than any wager.

452
00:34:23,260 --> 00:34:24,519
Play fast and loose with someone's heart,

453
00:34:25,719 --> 00:34:26,920
and when you lose,

454
00:34:27,739 --> 00:34:30,539
you lose for good.

455
00:34:34,360 --> 00:34:36,760
Make it high!

456
00:34:38,960 --> 00:34:39,960
Come on!

457
00:34:41,000 --> 00:34:43,739
Show the dice!

458
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:49,159
Yay!

459
00:34:56,280 --> 00:34:57,519
You place the bet,

460
00:35:00,579 --> 00:35:01,840
you take

461
00:35:01,840 --> 00:35:03,159
the hit.

462
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:34,400
Miss, it's late.

463
00:35:34,679 --> 00:35:36,380
Why strain your voice?

464
00:35:36,840 --> 00:35:37,619
Master Yu is here!

465
00:35:37,679 --> 00:35:38,980
He's sharing drinks with Mr. Jin.

466
00:35:42,059 --> 00:35:45,920
He hasn't stepped foot here

467
00:35:46,420 --> 00:35:49,480
for a year.

468
00:35:51,019 --> 00:35:52,559
Why should I care

469
00:35:53,639 --> 00:35:57,320
if he's here?

470
00:35:57,719 --> 00:35:59,340
Don't say that, Miss.

471
00:35:59,619 --> 00:36:01,179
The man runs an army.

472
00:36:01,360 --> 00:36:02,420
Aren't you glad

473
00:36:02,460 --> 00:36:03,619
he's here?

474
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:06,260
Get some rest.

475
00:36:06,440 --> 00:36:07,960
I will turn in shortly.

476
00:36:08,360 --> 00:36:09,159
Miss...

477
00:36:52,699 --> 00:36:53,739
Rough day?

478
00:36:54,159 --> 00:36:55,480
You're out later every night.

479
00:36:56,079 --> 00:36:57,900
Typhoid cases are spiking.

480
00:36:58,320 --> 00:36:59,719
We're drowning in sick kids.

481
00:37:00,679 --> 00:37:02,599
Why aren't you in bed?

482
00:37:05,960 --> 00:37:06,900
I was waiting for you.

483
00:37:09,639 --> 00:37:10,739
Don't wait up for me.

484
00:37:11,199 --> 00:37:13,179
Got an early shift tomorrow.

485
00:37:13,300 --> 00:37:14,320
Get some rest.

486
00:37:15,599 --> 00:37:16,500
It's bitter cold out.

487
00:37:16,840 --> 00:37:18,039
Let me drive you in the morning

488
00:37:18,619 --> 00:37:19,099
so you can

489
00:37:19,099 --> 00:37:20,380
get some shut-eye.

490
00:37:20,900 --> 00:37:22,000
Don't bother.

491
00:37:36,699 --> 00:37:38,360
[After you graduated,]

492
00:37:39,360 --> 00:37:40,500
[you took a job]

493
00:37:40,780 --> 00:37:43,000
[copying scripts at the Grand Vernal.]

494
00:37:43,800 --> 00:37:45,599
[We kinda rubbed each other]

495
00:37:46,179 --> 00:37:47,659
[the wrong way at first.]

496
00:37:48,500 --> 00:37:49,980
[Then fate stepped in.]

497
00:37:51,820 --> 00:37:52,800
[And eventually...]

498
00:37:53,739 --> 00:37:55,320
[we fell in love.]

499
00:38:03,320 --> 00:38:04,219
Still up?

500
00:38:08,659 --> 00:38:09,460
Don't tell me

501
00:38:10,400 --> 00:38:11,639
you forgot me again.

502
00:38:13,860 --> 00:38:14,739
No.

503
00:38:15,539 --> 00:38:16,800
You're Yu Changxuan.

504
00:38:24,260 --> 00:38:25,039
And?

505
00:38:35,059 --> 00:38:36,739
I've got something to ask.

506
00:38:37,840 --> 00:38:38,639
I'm all ears.

507
00:38:40,760 --> 00:38:42,099
I get that

508
00:38:42,099 --> 00:38:43,000
we're married,

509
00:38:44,340 --> 00:38:45,739
and I'm grateful

510
00:38:45,739 --> 00:38:47,139
you've been taking care of me.

511
00:38:48,099 --> 00:38:48,860
But

512
00:38:49,920 --> 00:38:51,159
my memory

513
00:38:51,159 --> 00:38:52,420
is gone.

514
00:38:52,960 --> 00:38:54,159
Can you give me

515
00:38:54,159 --> 00:38:55,360
a little time?

516
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:58,440
Time to get used to you...

517
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:00,179
to remember

518
00:39:00,179 --> 00:39:01,739
what we had.

519
00:39:02,440 --> 00:39:05,280
It'd make things

520
00:39:05,280 --> 00:39:06,659
a lot less awkward.

521
00:39:16,420 --> 00:39:17,039
Meaning?

522
00:39:19,519 --> 00:39:20,519
I can't...

523
00:39:22,840 --> 00:39:23,860
share a bedroom

524
00:39:23,860 --> 00:39:25,960
with you.

525
00:39:26,960 --> 00:39:29,940
Would you mind sleeping elsewhere?

526
00:39:48,460 --> 00:39:49,800
I slept on

527
00:39:50,860 --> 00:39:52,659
that field cot right there

528
00:39:53,539 --> 00:39:55,000
for two whole years,

529
00:39:56,940 --> 00:39:59,340
taking care of you

530
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:01,199
around the clock.

531
00:40:06,559 --> 00:40:07,360
What?

532
00:40:08,179 --> 00:40:09,539
Now that you're awake,

533
00:40:10,980 --> 00:40:12,219
you're kicking me to the curb?

534
00:40:13,980 --> 00:40:15,679
That's not what I meant...

535
00:40:23,539 --> 00:40:24,340
Hey, relax.

536
00:40:25,500 --> 00:40:26,519
Just messing with you.

537
00:40:45,099 --> 00:40:46,119
You could

538
00:40:46,460 --> 00:40:48,099
take another bedroom.

539
00:40:48,519 --> 00:40:49,480
You'd

540
00:40:49,820 --> 00:40:50,500
sleep better

541
00:40:50,500 --> 00:40:51,820
in a proper bed.

542
00:40:52,079 --> 00:40:53,159
You're not well yet.

543
00:40:53,159 --> 00:40:54,239
How could I leave you alone?

544
00:40:55,539 --> 00:40:57,519
Shout if you need anything at all.

545
00:40:57,800 --> 00:40:58,599
Don't be shy.

546
00:41:02,139 --> 00:41:02,940
Sweet dreams.

547
00:42:22,920 --> 00:42:24,039
[All these years,]

548
00:42:24,980 --> 00:42:26,500
[I dreamed of you opening your eyes.]

549
00:42:28,760 --> 00:42:30,239
[Now that you have,]

550
00:42:31,679 --> 00:42:33,460
[I don't know how to face you...]

551
00:43:34,539 --> 00:43:35,920
Heard you coughing earlier.

552
00:43:36,119 --> 00:43:37,300
Have some pear soup.

553
00:43:46,360 --> 00:43:47,079
Where's Tang?

554
00:43:47,920 --> 00:43:48,780
Why didn't she help?

555
00:43:50,860 --> 00:43:52,019
My grip's

556
00:43:52,019 --> 00:43:53,360
completely gone.

557
00:43:53,420 --> 00:43:54,780
Just wanted to push myself a bit...

558
00:44:02,000 --> 00:44:02,519
Allow me.

559
00:44:03,179 --> 00:44:03,920
I'm good...

560
00:44:05,579 --> 00:44:06,099
C'mon.

561
00:44:19,260 --> 00:44:20,039
Stay still...

562
00:44:39,840 --> 00:44:40,599
Hold still...

563
00:44:43,340 --> 00:44:44,780
Once you get your strength back,

564
00:44:46,219 --> 00:44:47,480
my maid duties are officially over.

565
00:45:05,719 --> 00:45:06,260
There.

566
00:45:17,199 --> 00:45:18,079
Doc says

567
00:45:18,159 --> 00:45:20,219
stringing beads gets the nerves firing again.

568
00:45:20,699 --> 00:45:21,800
Got a box right here for you.

569
00:45:22,340 --> 00:45:23,039
Thanks.

570
00:45:23,559 --> 00:45:24,179
No problem.

571
00:45:28,380 --> 00:45:29,059
Give it a shot.

572
00:45:54,760 --> 00:45:56,699
It's alright. C'mon.

573
00:46:17,960 --> 00:46:18,760
Take your time.

574
00:46:19,239 --> 00:46:20,039
I've got you.

575
00:47:12,099 --> 00:47:14,340
Ma'am, care for some cat's cradle?

576
00:47:16,380 --> 00:47:17,219
It helps your fingers...

577
00:47:29,679 --> 00:47:30,820
Fetch some roses.

578
00:47:31,500 --> 00:47:32,519
Master,

579
00:47:33,119 --> 00:47:33,980
the blooms aren't...

580
00:47:33,980 --> 00:47:34,460
Out.

581
00:47:43,239 --> 00:47:44,039
Why stop?

582
00:47:46,440 --> 00:47:46,960
Go on.
